I'll explore the current state of the teams feature — the store, components, and API layer — to understand what's connected and what's missing.Let me read the backend teams package (created previously), the store, and the remaining team components and API module patterns.Let me look at the project/ui/profiles store patterns to understand `$api` access and the surrounding conventions.Let me check the global mixins, app component registry, and how the `team` app/route resolves.Let me verify dependencies and the navigation/team wiring, plus the media store used by TeamView.I have the full picture now. Let me read the one file I only partially saw (`TeamChannelsSidebar.vue`) so I can reproduce it exactly.I now have a complete understanding of the codebase and the exact gap: the **team view is entirely wired to a `localStorage`-only Vuex store** (`src/store/teams.js`), while the backend exposes a `/api/teams` router with `Team`/`TeamMembers` models (created previously). There is **no frontend API module** for teams and the store never talks to the backend.

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
- Connect the team view to the backend API models: teams CRUD + membership, per project.
- Add the missing frontend API module (`src/api/modules/teams.js`) mirroring the backend router, and register it on the API object.
- Rewire `src/store/teams.js` so teams/members are loaded from and persisted to the API, while keeping the view-only state (colour, categories, channels, DMs, role/status) local.
- Finish the gaps: the backend `Team` model also carries **`profiles`** (AI profiles) — surface and manage them from the UI; make the now-async store calls awaited by the dialogs; keep teams in sync when the active project changes.

**Strategic Approach**
- Mirror existing patterns exactly: `src/api/modules/workspaces.js` (API module) + `src/api/api.js` lazy `get X()` (like `chats`); project-scoped access via `activeProject.$api.<module>` (like `chats`/`files`/`profiles`).
- Backend model is fixed (it lives outside the client tree), so map **backend `Team` ↔ UI team**:
  - `name`, `description`, `avatar→icon`, `profiles`, `tags` round-trip.
  - `users: [username]` → `members: [{id, username, role, status, joinedAt}]` (role/status stay local).
  - `color`, `categories`, `channels`, `directMessages` stay localStorage-only (channels are backed by chats).

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `$storex` must be imported in the store (like `chats.js`/`views.js`); it is only used inside actions.
- All API ops are best-effort with local fallback (offline still works, as today).
- Backend ignores client `id` on create → always adopt the server-assigned id.
- `DELETE /members` uses query params (axios DELETE bodies are unreliable); backend accepts both.
- Async store actions: `CreateTeamDialog`/`AddMemberDialog` must `await` (they only use the result to emit).

**Target Files**
- `src/api/modules/teams.js` — Create
- `src/api/api.js` — Modify (import + `teams` getter)
- `src/store/teams.js` — Modify (API wiring + profiles)
- `src/components/teams/CreateTeamDialog.vue` — Modify (await createTeam)
- `src/components/teams/AddMemberDialog.vue` — Modify (user/AI-profile toggle + await)
- `src/components/teams/TeamChannelsSidebar.vue` — Modify (AI Profiles section)
- `src/views/TeamView.vue` — Modify (reload teams on project change)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

1. **`api/modules/teams.js`** — list/get/create/update/delete + addMembers/removeMembers (profiles & users).
2. **`api/api.js`** — lazy `get teams()` + import.
3. **`store/teams.js`** — mapping helpers, `loadTeams`, async CRUD/members, `addProfile`/`removeProfile`, keep all local UI actions.
4. **`CreateTeamDialog.vue`** — `await` the async `createTeam`.
5. **`AddMemberDialog.vue`** — user/AI-profile switch; dispatch to `addMember`/`addProfile`.
6. **`TeamChannelsSidebar.vue`** — render `activeTeam.profiles` + remove.
7. **`TeamView.vue`** — watch `activeProject` → `loadTeams()`.

## 3. File Changes

